51:
"A young man met a girl one spring;
as anyone could see,
he was a bashful boy.

55:
Forgive me for this advice:
don't grieve for nothing;
you don't understand at all.

344:
Let it travel round the world;
I give this song to you,
this little song about five minutes.

349:
Five minutes, five minutes,
the clock will soon begin to chime;
make peace if you've quarreled.

350:
Our clock says five to twelve;
the New Year must already
be on its way.

353:
The New Year won't wait;
it's right outside the door.
Five minutes will fly by;
so little time is left.

360:
Five minutes is no time at all;
he's on the right path,
and it's a fine road.
